## Seed task

> {{SEED_TASK_PROMPT}}

Pick a task that exercises every layer: a real (not yet existing) feature that requires the agent to find auth helpers, find a domain model, and follow at least one convention rule. Keep it scoped to one or two files and ~50-100 lines of code change. Avoid tasks that need cross-file architectural decisions for the first run — those amplify variance.

## Procedure

### Baseline — rules and skills off

1. Temporarily rename `.cursor/rules/` → `.cursor/rules.disabled/` and `.cursor/skills/` → `.cursor/skills.disabled/`. (Keep `AGENTS.md` either way; it's the same in both runs.)
2. Restart Cursor (Cmd+Q and reopen) so the rule cache flushes.
3. Open a fresh chat in this repo.
4. Paste the seed task verbatim.
5. Capture metrics from Cursor's context panel and the agent transcript:

| Metric | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Total tool calls | {{N}} |
| Conversation tokens (this chat only) | {{N}}K |
| Total context at end | {{N}}K of 300K ({{PCT}}% full) |
| Wall-clock to first proposed diff | {{MM:SS}} |
| Did it grep for conventions? | {{Y/N}} |
| Produced a passing diff? | {{Y/N}} |

6. Restore the directories: `mv .cursor/rules.disabled .cursor/rules` and `mv .cursor/skills.disabled .cursor/skills`.

### Pipeline — rules and skills on

1. Confirm `.cursor/rules/` and `.cursor/skills/` are restored.
2. Restart Cursor again.
3. Open a fresh chat in this repo.
4. Paste the same seed task verbatim.
5. Capture the same metrics.

| Metric | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Total tool calls | {{N}} |
| Conversation tokens (this chat only) | {{N}}K |
| Total context at end | {{N}}K of 300K ({{PCT}}% full) |
| Wall-clock to first proposed diff | {{MM:SS}} |
| Skill activated | {{NAME_OR_NONE}} |
| Rule(s) activated (visible in context panel) | {{NAMES}} |
| Produced a passing diff? | {{Y/N}} |

